LAMMPS (4 Jul 2026 - Development - patch_4Jul2026-553-gc8348c2a23-modified)
KOKKOS mode with Kokkos version 5.1.99 is enabled
  using double precision
  using view layout = legacy
  will use up to 1 GPU(s) per node
  using 1 OpenMP thread(s) per MPI task
package kokkos
package kokkos newton on neigh half
# samQEq host-vs-device throughput benchmark: native SPC-FQ water (paper Section sec:water),
# base.data (512 molecules, equilibrated by in.equil) replicated REP^3 times.
#   -var REP n      replication per axis (2 -> 12,288 atoms; 4 -> 98,304; 6 -> 331,776; 8 -> 786,432)
#   -var NSTEP n    timed steps
#   -var DEV 0|1    1 = `fix_modify chg devsolve on` (KOKKOS binary only; the device charge solve)
#   -var ASPC 0|1   1 = `fix_modify chg aspc 2` (predictor-corrector); 0 = full solve every step
#   -var DUMP 0|1   1 = write per-atom charges at step 0 and at the last step (agreement check)
#   -var TAG s      label for the dump files
variable        REP   index 2
variable        NSTEP index 200
variable        DEV   index 0
variable        ASPC  index 0
variable        DUMP  index 0
variable        TAG   index run
units           metal
atom_style      full
boundary        p p p
special_bonds   lj/coul 1.0 1.0 1.0
read_data       base.data
Reading data file ...
  orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (24.8 24.8 24.8)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
  reading atoms ...
  1536 atoms
  reading velocities ...
  1536 velocities
  scanning bonds ...
  2 = max bonds/atom
  scanning angles ...
  1 = max angles/atom
  orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (24.8 24.8 24.8)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
  reading bonds ...
  1024 bonds
  reading angles ...
  512 angles
Finding 1-2 1-3 1-4 neighbors ...
  special bond factors lj:    1        1        1       
  special bond factors coul:  1        1        1       
     2 = max # of 1-2 neighbors
     2 = max # of special neighbors
  special bonds CPU = 0.001 seconds
  read_data CPU = 0.028 seconds
replicate       ${REP} ${REP} ${REP}
replicate       2 ${REP} ${REP}
replicate       2 2 ${REP}
replicate       2 2 2
Replication is creating a 2x2x2 = 8 times larger system...
  orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (49.6 49.6 49.6)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
  12288 atoms
  8192 bonds
  4096 angles
Finding 1-2 1-3 1-4 neighbors ...
  special bond factors lj:    1        1        1       
  special bond factors coul:  1        1        1       
     2 = max # of 1-2 neighbors
     2 = max # of special neighbors
  special bonds CPU = 0.003 seconds
  replicate CPU = 0.010 seconds
bond_style      zero
bond_coeff      1 1.0
angle_style     zero
angle_coeff     1 109.47
group           fq type 1 2
12288 atoms in group fq
pair_style      hybrid/overlay lj/cut 10.0 coul/long 10.0 coul/shield/intra 5.0 all
pair_coeff      1 1 lj/cut 0.01275 3.144
pair_coeff      1 2 lj/cut 0.0 1.0
pair_coeff      2 2 lj/cut 0.0 1.0
pair_coeff      * * coul/long
pair_coeff      * * coul/shield/intra 1.11
kspace_style    pppm/samqeq 1.0e-6
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
fix             chg fq qeq/sam 1 0.0 10.0 1.0e-5 spcfq_expt.param
if "${DEV} == 1" then "fix_modify chg devsolve on"
fix_modify chg devsolve on
samqeq/kk: S6 device solve ENABLED (engages on lr_ewald=0 + default gate)
if "${ASPC} == 1" then "fix_modify chg aspc 2"
fix             shk all shake 1.0e-4 100 0 b 1 a 1
Finding SHAKE clusters ...
       0 = # of size 2 clusters
       0 = # of size 3 clusters
       0 = # of size 4 clusters
    4096 = # of frozen angles
  find clusters CPU = 0.004 seconds
velocity        all create 298.0 4928459 mom yes rot yes dist gaussian loop geom
timestep        0.001
fix             nvt all nvt temp 298.0 298.0 0.1
thermo_style    custom step temp press pe etotal
thermo          50
if "${DUMP} == 1" then "dump qd all custom ${NSTEP} q_${TAG}.dump id q" "dump_modify qd sort id format float %.12g"
dump qd all custom ${NSTEP} q_${TAG}.dump id q
dump qd all custom 10 q_${TAG}.dump id q
dump qd all custom 10 q_agree_dev.dump id q
dump_modify qd sort id format float %.12g
run             ${NSTEP}
run             10

